WEBVTT

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.920
In the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, amen.

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:12.000
The reading from the Sinhaxadion, for May 27th, on which we commemorate our righteous

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:19.420
and God-bearing Father, John the Russian, Confessor and Wonderworker.

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:25.580
On the 27th of the month, we celebrate the memory of our venerable Father, John the Russian,

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:28.900
Confessor and Wonderworker.

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:34.740
Our Holy Father, John, was born in a village in Little Russia, and grew up in Piety and

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:37.940
love for the Holy Virtues.

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:43.820
Reaching adulthood at the time of the Russo-Turkish War in 1710, he enrolled in the Tsar's

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:51.220
Army, captured by the Tatters, he was sold to a Turkish cavalry officer who took him home

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:54.460
to Prokopion in Cappadocia.

00:00:54.460 --> 00:01:00.580
Like many of his companions in captivity who abjured Christianity, St. John resisted

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:07.420
both the suggestions and blows of his master, saying that no suffering could separate him from

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:09.420
the love of Christ.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:10.420
He added,

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:15.500
You are the master of my body, but not of my soul.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:21.100
If you leave me free to carry out my religious obligations, I will obey your orders with

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:22.660
alacrity.

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:28.100
It is a pleasure to me to sleep in this corner of your stable, thinking of Christ who considered

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:31.540
the manger in Bethlehem to be a royal bed.

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:37.580
I will endure without complaint your blows as the Lord endured those of the soldiers.

00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:42.620
I am ready to endure the greatest and most terrible torments if you want to submit me

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:47.340
to them, but I shall never deny Christ.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:52.860
These words, so full of Christian fervor, along with his chaste and humble behavior,

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:57.500
completely changed the heart and feelings of the Turkish officer towards him.

00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:03.220
He stopped tyrannizing over him and did not require him to deny his faith.

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:09.460
Given the task of looking after the horses, John lived in a dark corner of the stable, and

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:15.700
when his master rode out into the village, he had to follow him on foot like a slave.

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:21.020
The blessed man, however, accepted this degrading state with gratitude and glorified God

00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:24.260
for having thus delivered him from apostasy.

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:30.460
Barefoot, summer and winter, clad in rags and taking snatches of rest on the straw or the

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:38.260
dunghill like righteous Job, John did not in any way obeyed his exercises of devotion, and

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:43.660
he spent whole nights in prayer kneeling on the forecourt of the neighboring church of Saint

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:45.180
George.

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:50.220
He accepted without murmur the insults and mockery of the other slaves, and willingly

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:53.420
put himself at their service.

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:59.380
These sacrifices and striving in virtue were not without beneficial effects for his master,

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:04.100
who became the richest and most respected man in his town.

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:09.700
Having decided to make a pilgrimage to Mecca, obligatory for all devout Muslims, he reached

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:14.380
the holy city after a long, difficult journey.

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:19.820
Several weeks after his departure, his wife invited their kinsfolk and friends to a great

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:26.420
dinner so that the guests could express their hopes for her husband's safe return.

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:32.540
When John went into the room to serve a large pilaf, the mistress in the house exclaimed,

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:40.980
how its master would rejoice if he were here to eat this dish with us while it is so appetizing.

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:46.780
John with Drew a few moments in silent prayer, and then asked his mistress to give him a full

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:51.740
dish of the pilaf to send to his master in Mecca.

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:57.460
While all the guests were mocking him, the mistress of the house, smilingly, gave him a dish

00:03:57.460 --> 00:03:59.260
of the rice.

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:04.220
John went to the stable and raised the following prayer to God.

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:10.660
May he, who in former times, sent the prophet Habakkuk to Babylon to carry food to the prophet

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:18.140
Daniel in the lion's den, give ear also to my prayer and bring this dish to my master.

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:25.420
He then returned to the banqueting hall and announced that the dish had arrived at its destination.

00:04:25.420 --> 00:04:31.620
Everyone present burst out laughing and accused him of being secretly fooled to replicion.

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:36.900
However, when the master returned from his journey, bringing with him the empty dish bearing

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:42.660
his initials and told how he had found it full of a delicious pilaf one evening when

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:49.620
he returned to his tent, everyone in the house was stupified, and invoking Allah began to

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:54.300
accord honor and great respect to the Christian slave.

00:04:54.300 --> 00:05:01.260
They offered to give him his freedom and a more worthy chamber, but St. John refused, saying

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:06.380
that he preferred to remain in the dark corner of the stable where he could better glorify

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:07.780
God.

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:11.420
He thus lived a devout life for several years.

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:17.580
When he fell ill, he asked that a priest bring him holy communion, but the priest, afraid

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:24.700
to take the sacrament into a Muslim house, hid it in an apple and gave it to the saint.

00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:30.940
Thus St. John received the viaticum of eternal life and fell asleep in peace to obtain the

00:05:30.940 --> 00:05:38.460
glorious liberty of the children of God on the 27th of May in 1730.

00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:45.060
Three years later, an elderly priest and some other Christians several times saw at night

00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:49.940
a pillar of fire that descended from heaven onto the saint's tomb.

00:05:49.940 --> 00:05:56.060
They opened it and found their his incorrupt body, giving off a sweet fragrance.

00:05:56.060 --> 00:06:00.500
They then took it with great rejoicing to the Church of St. George and placed it in

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:03.580
a reliquary under the altar.

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:07.660
From then on the precious relics worked the great number of miracles for the Christians of

00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:11.940
Cappadocia and even for the Muslims.

00:06:11.940 --> 00:06:16.980
During the sacking of the village by the troops of Osman Pasha, the relics were burned by the

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:23.020
Turkish soldiers, but they remained untouched, and the saint appeared in the midst of the

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:26.860
flames, threatening the infidel soldiers.

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:31.780
The terrified Turks abandoned all their spoils and fled from the village.

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:36.780
On another occasion, the saint appeared to hold up with his own hands the roof of the

00:06:36.780 --> 00:06:43.340
Greek school that was collapsing, thus saving the 20 children who were inside.

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:49.380
At the time of the expulsion of the Greeks from Asia Minor in 1922, the Christians of Procopion

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:52.140
took these holy relics with them to Greece.

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:58.180
To the village of Neoprocopion on the island of Elbea as their greatest treasure.

00:06:58.180 --> 00:07:05.580
St. John has, since then, been venerated as a limitless source of healing and blessing

00:07:05.580 --> 00:07:10.990
by all who draw near to him with faith.

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:16.670
Through the prayers of our holy fathers, O Lord Jesus Christ our God, have mercy on us

00:07:16.670 --> 00:07:17.670
and save us.
